# Generated by Cargo. Anchored to the repo root with a leading slash: unanchored
# `target` would also ignore any directory named `target` nested anywhere, which
# is a real hazard once assets/ and shaders/ exist.
/target
/debug

# Tool-owned local state. Holds the cooked asset cache, which is generated from
# `assets/` and keyed by content hash -- see DESIGN.md 2.8 and CONVENTIONS.md 1.
# Committing cooked output is how it silently goes stale against its source.
.slop/

# Third-party test assets, fetched by `slop-cli fetch` rather than committed.
# Sponza alone is 51 MB across 71 files, and a binary that large is permanent
# once it is in git history -- every future clone pays for it forever. Anything
# under here is reproducible from an upstream URL, so the repo records how to get
# it instead of the bytes themselves. See DESIGN.md 2.8.
/assets/vendor/

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
